  m_Name: Object_254
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Valve Stem
  description: The Valve Stem is a tiny, elongated component located at the top-center-center
    of the engine, made of Frame material, which serves as the shaft that connects
    the valve to the camshaft. Its primary function is to transmit the rotational
    motion of the camshaft to the valve, enabling it to open and close, and a notable
    aspect is that it is designed to withstand the high stresses and loads associated
    with engine operation. The valve stem's tiny size and elongated shape allow it
    to fit within the engine's compact valve train.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
